Provenance rescue (not in the commit message, which is about the artifact viewer):

This commit also carries an unrelated correctness fix in
nvidia/cmd/cudaprof/view_nvrtc.go -- the nvrtcx.WithNoCache() option on the
recompile path, and its comment. That fix is why the NVRTC flag comparison
panel reports honest numbers.

The defect: the nvrtcx content-addressed cache served CUBINs that no fresh
compile produces. Measured against NVRTC 13.0 on ds4_math.cu, fresh compiles
of base, --ftz=true, --prec-div=false, --prec-sqrt=false and
--extra-device-vectorization all yield CUBIN 7f5d5871d61abd48 (2305256 bytes),
reproducibly across separate processes -- those four flags are no-ops on that
source. Served from the cache, base gave 5f450e62 (2305232) and the four gave a
shared 05d18dcd (2338920), and the panel reported them removing 24 FCHK and 8
MUFU.RCP. The tell was four unrelated flags agreeing to the instruction.

A comparison that invents a difference is worse than a slow one, so every
variant on this path is compiled fresh. After the fix, --ftz=true honestly
shows 81 changed PTX opcodes (fma.rn.f32 1421->0, fma.rn.ftz.f32 0->1498) and
zero changed SASS rows.

Found and fixed by: claude-code model=Opus 5 (1M context) session=d56928ce-d6c4-4edb-bd73-c2762257b8f8 iterm_session_id=FE9C2856-3582-4573-899B-332048F9D406 date=2026-09-15

CORRECTION (same author, later the same day) to the paragraph above.

The claim that those four flags 'are no-ops on that source' is WRONG, and so is
treating the fresh compile as ground truth. Compiling the same 83695 bytes with
nvcc -arch=sm_121: base FFMA=2686 FFMA.FTZ=0 FCHK=190; --ftz=true FFMA=996
FFMA.FTZ=1850 FCHK=166. nvcc rewrites 1850 instructions.

NVRTC 13.0 does not. It accepts --ftz=true, applies it to the PTX it returns
(fma.rn.ftz.f32 1498, fma.rn.f32 0), and returns a CUBIN byte-identical to the
unflagged one. NVRTC's PTX and its own CUBIN disagree on the same compile.
Reproduced with a bare nvrtc.CreateProgram probe, no nvrtcx and no cache, so it
is NVRTC behavior, not a wrapper or cache artifact. --use_fast_math is honored
all the way to SASS (FFMA.FTZ 1743, FCHK 190->0); the individual flags it
implies are not.

What survives: the cache defect is real and independent. The cached path served
ONE shared CUBIN for four distinct option sets while base got another. Four
unrelated flags cannot agree to the instruction -- that is a keying bug, and
WithNoCache is a correct mitigation for it. What does not survive is the
inference that the fresh result is therefore correct; it is only self-consistent.

Consequence for the viewer: for a flag NVRTC honors only in PTX, the SASS tier
shows zero changed rows and reads as 'this flag does nothing' when nvcc says
otherwise. PTX differing while SASS does not is the signature of a flag NVRTC
dropped, not evidence that the flag is inert.

